  <section class="section section-soft stripe-top" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
    <div class="container--narrow">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="intro-title">What is a vehicle wrap?</h2>
      <p>A vehicle wrap is self-adhesive cast vinyl applied to the bodywork of a car, van or light truck. The vehicle becomes a mobile billboard visible to anyone in the street, on the motorway or at the customer's doorstep. Three formats are common. <strong>Partial lettering</strong> places logo, phone number and website on the side panels and rear door. <strong>Partial wrap</strong> covers selected panels in solid colour with overlaid lettering and graphics. <strong>Full wrap</strong> covers every visible body panel and lets you change the base colour of the vehicle entirely.</p>

      <p>For most Rotterdam SMEs a partial lettering or partial wrap delivers the best return. It is cheaper to produce, faster to install, and still highly visible from a distance. A full wrap makes sense when the vehicle is also the brand &mdash; food trucks, festival vans, premium service vehicles, customer-facing fleet.</p>

      <h3 style="margin-top:var(--space-6);">Materials we use</h3>
      <ul style="list-style:disc; padding-left:var(--space-5); color:var(--ink-muted); line-height:var(--lh-base); margin-top:var(--space-3);">
        <li style="margin-bottom:var(--space-3);"><strong style="color:var(--ink);">3M IJ-series with 3M overlaminate</strong> &mdash; the industry-standard combination. UV-stable for seven years, conforms to compound curves, removes cleanly.</li>
        <li style="margin-bottom:var(--space-3);"><strong style="color:var(--ink);">Avery Dennison MPI 1105 with DOL laminate</strong> &mdash; premium alternative with stronger conformability for vans with deep recesses and rivets.</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--ink);">Hexis Skintac</strong> &mdash; European cast vinyl, suitable for specialist colours and short-run promotional wraps.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

